<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nazism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as National Socialism</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nazism, or National <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socialism">Socialism</a>, was the far-right ideology of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a>'s party, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1933 to 1945. It combined extreme nationalism, racism and antisemitism with authoritarian rule. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> link its rise to the humiliations and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a> imposed after the empire's defeat in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nazism.jpg" alt="Nazism" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Institut_f%C3%BCr_Sexualwissenschaft_-_Bibliothek_1933.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
